course: dictionary
lesson: 9983
title: Teat, a word from the farm and the nursery
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are easier to understand when you know where they are used. Teat is one of them. «A cow is milked from her four teats.» The sentence tells you the cow gives her milk from her teats, so a teat must be a part of an animal that makes or gives milk.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «Each piglet picks its own teat and goes back to it every feed.» A feed is a meal of milk for a baby animal, so a teat is the part the baby sucks to get milk. Check your meaning: "each piglet picks its own milk part" still makes sense, so you are on the right track.
explain: Teat also has a meaning at home. «The baby pulled on the bottle teat» means the rubber or plastic top of a baby's bottle. The same idea works here too: the baby sucks it to get milk. When one word has two meanings, the words around it show you which one is meant.
fact: A teat is the small, soft part on a female mammal's body that her babies suck to get milk.
fact: Cows, goats, sheep and pigs all have teats.
fact: «A sow, a mother pig, can have a litter of a dozen piglets or more born together.»
fact: A teat is also the rubber or plastic top of a baby's bottle.
fact: Each piglet picks a teat and goes back to the same one at every feed.
exercise: «A cow is milked from her four teats.» What is a teat? | A bucket for carrying water | A type of grass in the field | *The small part a baby sucks to get milk | A kind of hat worn on the farm
exercise: «A milking robot finds the four teats and fixes the cups on.» What does the robot find? | Four windows | Four wheels | *Four teats | Four bells
exercise: Ella's baby brother drinks from his bottle. Which part of the bottle does he suck? | The bottom | The handle | *The teat | The label
test: «A sow usually has about 8 to 12 piglets.» What is a sow? | Teat | Ewe | Piglet | *A mother pig
test: What is a teat for? | To make the mother grunt | To keep the mother warm in winter | To hold food for the mother | *To give milk to a baby
exam: Mia reads «the cow's teats» and «bottle teat». Which phrase means the top of a baby's bottle? | the cow's teats | a sheep's fleece | *bottle teat | a sow's litter
